    "narrative": "Today\u2019s slate for **Ghost Ride the WHIP** is headlined by **Corbin Carroll**, who carries our highest daily efficiency score of 75.69. While Kevin Gausman is a formidable arm, the combination of **Corbin Carroll**\u2019s projected role in the #2 hole and the matchup against a pitcher with a \"slow delivery\" profile provides a significant boost to his stolen base equity\u2014a critical multiplier in our 5x5 Roto strategy. **Seiya Suzuki** also emerges as a high-floor play at 71.14; assuming he slots into the #2 spot, he feasts on the exploitable 5.27 xERA of Merrill Kelly, benefitting from a massive 19% boost due to the SP skill disparity. Meanwhile, **Henry Bolte** (61.01) and **Mickey Moniak** (60.01) provide strong outfield production, with **Henry Bolte** gaining significant value from his leadoff spot and a park factor conducive to his profile.\n\nThe most difficult bench decision involved **Cole Young**, whose 33.14 score landed him well below our 40-point \"zebra\" floor. Despite a promising offensive profile, the matchup against Wheeler\u2014a pitcher with a sub-3.10 xERA\u2014coupled with a bottom-third batting order assignment and the defensive impact of an elite opposing catcher, forced him to the pine. We are exercising caution with **Josh Naylor** (48.34) and **Zach McKinstry** (40.17) today as well; both are skating near the edge of our viability threshold. **Zach McKinstry** remains in the lineup purely due to favorable wind conditions offsetting a difficult matchup against Rasmussen, but he is a candidate for a late-game swap if the lineup shifts negatively. \n\nWe continue to monitor the status of **James Wood**, whose absence due to injury remains a significant drag on our outfield depth, forcing reliance on streamers like **Mickey Moniak**. While we have a robust bench including **Tyler Soderstrom**, **Vinnie Pasquantino**, **Jose Caballero**, **Austin Riley**, **Giancarlo Stanton**, **Trevor Story**, **Brice Turang**, **Isaac Paredes**, **Dalton Rushing**, **Griffin Conine**, **Edwin Arroyo**, and **Travis Bazzana**, today's matchups largely favor our starters. We will keep a close watch on **Seiya Suzuki**'s confirmation for the #2 spot; if that lineup order fluctuates, his value-add will compress rapidly, potentially shifting our internal calculus for the late-afternoon games.",
